BUNKERGAME OVERNIGHT WORLD BUILD V2

You are the primary BunkerGame Art Director / orchestrator.

This is a REAL implementation run, not a planning exercise and not a proof-only exercise.

You must build a substantial playable world for BunkerGame overnight and continue autonomously until the required integrated checkpoints pass or a genuine unrecoverable blocker remains after five recovery attempts.

============================================================
MISSION
============================================================

Build a large, cohesive, creepy survival-world environment appropriate for BunkerGame.

The finished world should feel significantly larger, richer and more alive than the current prototype.

Use the existing approved assets and asset families wherever suitable.

Create additional assets only when existing approved assets are insufficient.

The world should include, where appropriate:

- substantial traversable terrain;
- hills and elevation variation;
- valleys, slopes and natural landforms;
- dense and sparse forest regions;
- believable tree distribution rather than uniform grids;
- rocks and boulder fields;
- natural landmarks;
- paths and navigational clearings;
- bunker/facility integration;
- meaningful spawn region;
- vegetation;
- environmental storytelling;
- distant ambient wildlife;
- animals moving in the background where technically practical;
- creepy atmospheric environmental motion;
- world ambience;
- lighting;
- fog/atmosphere;
- environmental audio;
- gameplay-relevant resource placement;
- scripts required for new systems;
- technical validation;
- controlled Play testing;
- debugging and fixes.

The result must remain a survival game world, not merely a visual demo.

============================================================
CANONICAL ORCHESTRATION
============================================================

The required orchestration is:

Muse / bunkergame-art-director
    ->
Qwen / bunkergame-master-reasoner
    ->
MiMo / bunker-builder
    ->
Roblox Studio native Assistant generation/composition
    +
BloxForge engineering validation
    ->
Muse visual review
    ->
filesystem/Rojo persistence
    ->
Studio verification
    ->
Play QA
    ->
final review

Never claim any participant was invoked unless it was actually invoked.

For reusable visual assets:

1. Search the approved Asset Library first.
2. Reuse existing approved assets/families when adequate.
3. Prefer LIBRARY_REFERENCE when an existing approved asset is sufficiently close.
4. Otherwise use USER_REFERENCE, QWEN_GENERATED_REFERENCE or ONLINE_REFERENCE when appropriate.
5. Roblox Assistant performs native creative generation/composition.
6. BloxForge performs engineering QA.
7. Muse performs visual review after visual evidence exists.
8. Only approved reusable assets are registered.
9. Persist approved reusable assets before depending on them permanently.

============================================================
CRITICAL SAFETY RULES
============================================================

DO NOT run `rojo serve`.

DO NOT start a live Rojo synchronization session.

DO NOT allow destructive Rojo reconciliation.

DO NOT use /tmp for evidence, state, generated prompts, builds or temporary project artifacts.

All generated evidence must remain under:

/Users/Ori/Documents/Projects/BunkerGame/.opencode/overnight_world_v2

Filesystem + Rojo source remains the permanent source of truth.

However, NEVER delete Studio-only content merely because it differs from filesystem.

Before deleting, replacing, reconciling or superseding any existing Studio content:

1. inspect it;
2. determine whether it is reusable;
3. preserve useful assets;
4. persist anything worth keeping;
5. only then perform controlled replacement.

Never perform broad destructive cleanup simply to make Studio match Rojo.

`rojo build` and `rojo sourcemap` are allowed for validation.

Use canonical Rojo:

/Users/Ori/.aftman/bin/rojo

Do not use another Rojo installation.

============================================================
CHECKPOINT SYSTEM
============================================================

You MUST use this command at every checkpoint:

.opencode/overnight_world_v2/checkpoint.sh CHECKPOINT STATUS "message"

Valid STATUS values:

START
INFO
PASS
FAIL

Do not merely print fake checkpoint strings.

You MUST actually invoke checkpoint.sh so a physical checkpoint event exists.

Use exactly these major checkpoints:

CP01_SAFETY
CP02_WORLD_PLAN
CP03_TERRAIN
CP04_FOREST
CP05_ROCKS_LANDMARKS
CP06_WILDLIFE
CP07_GAMEPLAY
CP08_PRESENTATION
CP09_TECH_QA
CP10_PLAY_QA
CP11_VISUAL_QA
CP12_FINAL

============================================================
CP01_SAFETY
============================================================

Start with:

.opencode/overnight_world_v2/checkpoint.sh CP01_SAFETY START "Inspecting existing world and preserving safety boundary"

Inspect:

- current filesystem;
- current Studio;
- current world hierarchy;
- approved GeneratedAssets;
- Asset Library;
- existing spawn;
- terrain;
- existing gameplay-critical anchors;
- existing trees;
- existing rocks;
- bunker/facility;
- current Studio mode.

Do not delete anything.

Confirm Studio is Edit mode before implementation.

Create a baseline understanding of what already exists and what can be reused.

PASS only when the implementation boundary is understood.

============================================================
CP02_WORLD_PLAN
============================================================

Invoke the real Qwen master-reasoner.

Qwen must reason about:

- overall world topology;
- scale;
- player navigation;
- sightlines;
- bunker relationship to exterior;
- safe spawn;
- forest density;
- hill placement;
- landmark distribution;
- wildlife zones;
- resource zones;
- horror pacing;
- performance boundaries.

The planned map should be large enough to feel substantial but practical for Roblox.

Avoid giant empty terrain.

Create purposeful density gradients.

PASS after the world topology has been selected and implementation can proceed.

============================================================
CP03_TERRAIN
============================================================

Build or substantially improve terrain.

Requirements:

- real elevation variation;
- hills;
- valleys or depressions;
- slopes;
- clear traversable routes;
- bunker/spawn integration;
- no obvious terrain walls trapping players;
- no giant flat empty plate;
- no extreme cliff maze unless intentional;
- appropriate boundaries.

Use deterministic source-controlled systems where practical.

Inspect results in Studio.

PASS only after terrain exists and is navigable.

============================================================
CP04_FOREST
============================================================

Search Asset Library before creating new trees.

Reuse existing approved tree assets and families wherever possible.

Build a convincing forest system with:

- varied density;
- forest clusters;
- clearings;
- young/mature variation where available;
- edge transitions;
- natural randomization;
- no visible grid distribution;
- no tree intersections with critical navigation;
- no trees blocking bunker doors;
- sensible performance limits.

If new reusable trees are required:

Qwen reference decision
->
Roblox Assistant native generation
->
BloxForge technical QA
->
Muse review
->
Asset Library registration
->
filesystem persistence.

PASS only after the world has substantial forest coverage and navigation remains usable.

============================================================
CP05_ROCKS_LANDMARKS
============================================================

Reuse approved boulder and rock assets first.

Add:

- individual boulders;
- rock clusters;
- terrain-supported formations;
- landmarks;
- visual navigation anchors;
- composition around paths and bunker approaches.

Avoid random prop spam.
